  "base": "af34a54e",
  "claims": [
    "Composite identification uses the confirmed, alethic, preferred external uniqueness anchored on the entity, with the smallest sorted role references winning a tie, independent of declaration order (RR1, F1).",
    "Duplicate uniqueness constraints form one key, preferred if any is, and share one disposition; unique keys sort by column position (RR2, RR3).",
    "An external uniqueness whose columns lie in one table is a unique key, and an objectified uniqueness narrower than the key is a unique key (RR4, RR5).",
    "Under ALTERNATE an inheriting subtype keeps its foreign key to its supertype's table; a role played by a value type with a table is a foreign key; an absorbed unary column is nullable (RR6-RR8).",
    "map_model never raises for a model the loader admits, dispositions has exactly one row per fact type and constraint, and mapping time stays linear, including composite identification (C1, C2, C5, F9)."
  ],
